  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRRS (DRR) Libya 2023 (DRRS24LY03)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">After storm Daniel made landfall in Libya an unprecedented amount of rain has fallen in the eastern part of Libya. This has caused extreme river flows and subsequent dam failures.The government of Libya has requested international assistance through its embassy in the Hague, which again reached the DRRS team through the Netherlands embassy in Tripoli, Libya.In an effort to be as effective as possible, the Netherlands embassy in Tripoli, Libya together with the DRRS team, has joined forces with the World Bank in their Rapid Damage and Needs Assessment (RDNA) work.Building on the RDNA, the team will work on a comprehensive report for the Derna dam failure, as well as a visualisation of the event.On a broader level, input will be given for a national dam assessment.</narrative>
  </description>
